  "decision_conditions": [
    "Due\r\nto the existing road layout, including the presence of a central island, the\r\nproposal would give rise to conditions prejudicial to the free flow of traffic\r\nand to the general safety of both vehicular and pedestrian movement on the\r\npublic highway. The arrangement would therefore be contrary to Policy T6 of the\r\nLondon Plan (2021) and Policies T16.1, T16.2, T16.3 and T16.4 of the Merton\r\nLocal Plan (2024)\r\n\r\n",
    "The\r\nsafe operation of the proposed access is dependent on only one vehicle being\r\nparked on the frontage at any one time and on vehicles entering and exiting the\r\nsite in forward gear with on‑site turning. The Council cannot reasonably impose\r\nor enforce conditions restricting the number of vehicles parked on private\r\nland, nor can it secure forward‑gear access or on‑site turning through\r\ncondition. In the absence of any enforceable mechanism to ensure these\r\nessential safety requirements, the proposal would result in unsafe manoeuvring\r\nand would be prejudicial to the free flow of traffic and the safety of all\r\nhighway users. The development is therefore contrary to Policy T6 of the London\r\nPlan (2021) and Policies T16.1, T16.2, T16.3 and T16.4 of the Merton Local Plan\r\n(2024)"
  ],
